Ocelith is the curator of the library at [[Org/The Harlequins/Harlequin Town|Harlequin Town]] aboard the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]. He is a great creature of bone, like a dragon and an armadillo at once, with fangs and claws and spines along his back that move as he chooses. He turns his head a full half circle without shifting his body, and reads from a giant desk held off the floor by enormous hands that grow up out of the stone.

He keeps the town's books and a long map of the horizon voidward. He is cheerful and flattering, fond of hearing that he is well read, and dismissive of the six gods. He says plainly that he is not a bone devil.

His desk holds a typewriter, and the ink ribbon the Party brought back fits it: an inch-wide strip of fabric dyed red, kept close enough that its theft was worth the trouble it caused. He lends books on an index card in the cover, signed with a name and a date, so that a book that passes from hand to hand can be traced home. He says the Harlequins are a commune with no need for money, and has no other errand for the Party for now.
